# Edera zone kernel variant: CPU mitigations compiled out.
#
# CONFIG_CPU_MITIGATIONS is the master switch; all CONFIG_MITIGATION_* symbols
# depend on it, so olddefconfig drops them together and there is no need to list
# each one. Compiling them out (rather than booting mitigations=off) also removes
# the entry/exit stubs, so it is strictly cheaper than the runtime knob.
#
# Sound ONLY when the whole zone is a single trust domain running no untrusted
# in-guest code: the hypervisor boundary provides cross-zone isolation, and these
# mitigations defend against speculative leaks *inside* a shared kernel. This is a
# deliberate security downgrade and must not be published or CI-wired without
# security sign-off.
# CONFIG_CPU_MITIGATIONS is not set
